.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-config-profile-delete 1  "rev-stealth-config-profile-delete " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-profile\-delete \- Best\-effort overwrite\-then\-delete (`shred\-like`) for the profile directory. Refuses if the profile is currently active per `$REV_SCRAPING_HOME` resolution
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config profile delete\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Best\-effort overwrite\-then\-delete (shred\-like) for the profile directory. Refuses if the profile is currently active (per $REV_SCRAPING_HOME resolution). \-\-yes is required for non\-interactive deletion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Required for non\-interactive deletion. Without it we exit 2 with an error so an operator typo cannot wipe a profile
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Profile name to remove
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config profile delete work \-\-yes
  $ rev\-stealth config profile delete demo\-2026 \-\-yes

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Profile removed.
  1  UserError        Missing \-\-yes / active profile / name not found.
  3  PermanentError   shred IO failure.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_HOME            Override `~/.rev_scraping/` base.
  REV_SCRAPING_PROFILES_ROOT   Override the profiles root directory.
